    "narrative": "The priority for Ghost Ride the WHIP today centers on the elite speed-power profile of **Corbin Carroll** (77.71), whose favorable matchup against Phillips and the added boost of leading off in the two-hole make him our premier start. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) remains a primary cornerstone; the combination of a favorable wind out and a robust 11% SP skill advantage against Rocker cements his status as a must-start. Additionally, **Seiya Suzuki** (71.16) and **Josh Naylor** (69.80) are positioned for high-upside games, with park factors in their respective venues significantly elevating their raw projections. While **Austin Riley** (65.27) is starting against the lefty Kay, the 19% SP skill edge provides enough cushion to negate any platoon concerns, keeping him firmly in the strong category.\n\nOur bench strategy remains tethered to health and scheduling, as **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Jose Caballero** are unavailable due to team off-days, while **Mickey Moniak** remains sidelined on the IL. Consequently, our bottom-tier starters like **Zach McKinstry** (44.30) and **Alex Freeland** (47.93) are pressed into service by default, despite their marginal daily efficiency scores. **Cole Young** (52.70) presents a unique case; while his high park factor is inviting, the presence of the formidable Bradish forces a cautious outlook, though his slot at the top of the order mitigates the risk. With the roster depth currently depleted by off-days and injuries, we are leaning heavily on **Gabriel Moreno** (60.46) to anchor the catcher position, keeping a close watch on **Dalton Rushing** (51.68) as he faces the risk of batting eighth against Keller. We remain prepared to pivot if any late-scratch news arises for **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, **Kyle Karros**, **Carson Williams**, or **Travis Bazzana** if their respective lineups materialize with shifting order dynamics.",
